{"cartConfigs":{"isActive":false},"dynamic_pages":[],"options":{"mobileOnly":false,"versionID":null},"page":[{"id":"sec_2101","type":"section","responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"background":"rgba(255,255,255,1)","height":72}},"mobile":{"styles":{"background":"rgba(255,255,255,1)","height":66}}},"children":[{"id":"t_2102","type":"text-block","specials":{"text":"<a href=\"https://www.dijaedadula.com/home\" style=\"color:rgba(26,26,26,1);text-decoration:none\">DIJAE DADULA</a>"},"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(26,26,26,1)","fontSize":16,"fontWeight":"800","height":24,"left":160,"letterSpacing":"3px","lineHeight":"1.4","top":26,"width":260}},"mobile":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(26,26,26,1)","fontSize":14,"fontWeight":"800","height":22,"left":20,"letterSpacing":"2px","lineHeight":"1.4","top":22}}}},{"id":"b_2103","type":"button","specials":{"text":"Book a call"},"events":[{"action":"open_link","id":"ev_2104","target":"https://www.dijaedadula.com/book","targetURL":"_self","type":"click"}],"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"background":"rgba(0,122,102,1)","borderRadius":"8px","color":"rgba(255,255,255,1)","fontSize":15,"fontWeight":"700","height":40,"left":650,"textAlign":"center","top":16}},"mobile":{"styles":{"background":"rgba(0,122,102,1)","borderRadius":"8px","color":"rgba(255,255,255,1)","fontSize":14,"fontWeight":"700","height":38,"left":270,"textAlign":"center","top":14,"width":130}}}},{"id":"n_2105","type":"text-block","specials":{"text":"<a href=\"https://grow.dijaedadula.com/newsletter\" style=\"color:rgba(26,26,26,1);text-decoration:none\">Newsletter</a>"},"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(26,26,26,1)","fontSize":15,"fontWeight":"500","height":24,"left":532,"lineHeight":"1.4","textAlign":"center","top":26,"width":110}},"mobile":{"config":{"hide":true},"styles":{"color":"rgba(26,26,26,1)","fontSize":14,"height":22,"left":270,"lineHeight":"1.4","textAlign":"center","top":22,"width":130}}}},{"id":"n_2106","type":"text-block","specials":{"text":"<a href=\"https://www.dijaedadula.com/blog\" style=\"color:rgba(26,26,26,1);text-decoration:none\">Blog</a>"},"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(26,26,26,1)","fontSize":15,"fontWeight":"500","height":24,"left":414,"lineHeight":"1.4","textAlign":"center","top":26,"width":110}},"mobile":{"config":{"hide":true},"styles":{"color":"rgba(26,26,26,1)","fontSize":14,"height":22,"left":270,"lineHeight":"1.4","textAlign":"center","top":22,"width":130}}}},{"id":"l_2107","type":"line","responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"borderColor":"rgba(230,232,236,1)","left":0,"top":63,"width":960}},"mobile":{"styles":{"borderColor":"rgba(230,232,236,1)","left":0,"top":60,"width":420}}}}]},{"id":"sec_2108","type":"section","responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"background":"rgba(255,255,255,1)","height":9715}},"mobile":{"styles":{"background":"rgba(255,255,255,1)","height":12231}}},"children":[{"id":"t_2109","type":"text-block","specials":{"text":"<a href=\"https://www.dijaedadula.com/blog\" style=\"color:rgba(0,122,102,1);text-decoration:underline\">Blog</a> · CRM and automation that sells"},"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(120,120,120,1)","fontSize":14,"fontWeight":"400","height":25,"left":160,"lineHeight":"1.5","textAlign":"left","top":64,"width":640}},"mobile":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(120,120,120,1)","fontSize":13,"fontWeight":"400","height":24,"left":20,"lineHeight":"1.5","textAlign":"left","top":48,"width":380}}}},{"id":"t_2110","type":"text-block","specials":{"tag":"h1","text":"AI Automation for Clinics and Med Spas: Bookings, Reminders and Reviews"},"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(26,26,26,1)","fontSize":42,"fontWeight":"800","height":154,"left":160,"lineHeight":"1.18","textAlign":"left","top":105,"width":640}},"mobile":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(26,26,26,1)","fontSize":30,"fontWeight":"800","height":112,"left":20,"lineHeight":"1.18","textAlign":"left","top":84,"width":380}}}},{"id":"t_2111","type":"text-block","specials":{"text":"Most clinics lose patients after the inquiry, not before it. Here is where automation closes the gaps, what must stay with your team, and how to launch it safely."},"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(85,85,85,1)","fontSize":21,"fontWeight":"400","height":98,"left":160,"lineHeight":"1.5","textAlign":"left","top":277,"width":640}},"mobile":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(85,85,85,1)","fontSize":18,"fontWeight":"400","height":112,"left":20,"lineHeight":"1.5","textAlign":"left","top":210,"width":380}}}},{"id":"t_2112","type":"text-block","specials":{"text":"By <a href=\"https://www.dijaedadula.com/home\" style=\"color:rgba(0,122,102,1);text-decoration:underline\">Dijae Dadula</a> · October 15, 2026 · 9 min read"},"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(120,120,120,1)","fontSize":14,"fontWeight":"400","height":25,"left":160,"lineHeight":"1.5","textAlign":"left","top":393,"width":640}},"mobile":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(120,120,120,1)","fontSize":13,"fontWeight":"400","height":24,"left":20,"lineHeight":"1.5","textAlign":"left","top":336,"width":380}}}},{"id":"eb_2120","type":"editor-blog","specials":{"html":"<div class='dd-article'>\n<figure class='dd-fig'><div class='dd-shot' style='aspect-ratio:16/9'><img src='https://statics.pancake.vn/web-media-264/47/1e/9d/dd/f3ffded56dbdc513f45bdcd734c55fbb16c1cd38ae5a0516d5f521cc.png' alt='Illustration of a med spa reception with a phone showing a chat and a booked calendar slot, a robot assistant ringing a reminder bell and a five-star review card' width='1536' height='864' loading='lazy'></div></figure>\n<p>Most clinics and med spas do not have a marketing problem. They have a follow-through problem. The ads work and the inquiries arrive, but the reply comes hours later, booking takes five messages, patients forget their appointment, and happy clients are never asked for a review. Every one of those gaps costs a booking you already paid to get.</p>\n<p>This guide is for clinic owners, med spa managers and the agencies that serve them. It shows where automation fits across the patient journey, what to automate first, what must stay with your team, and how to stay on the right side of privacy and review rules.</p>\n<div class='dd-tldr'>\n<p class='dd-tldr-title'>What you will get</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The <b>four places</b> clinics lose patients between the first message and the next booking.</li>\n<li>What an AI agent <b>should and should not</b> answer in a clinic.</li>\n<li>A <b>reminder schedule</b> backed by research on no-shows.</li>\n<li>A <b>review and rebooking flow</b> that follows Google's rules.</li>\n<li>A <b>launch test checklist</b> and the metrics to track.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<nav class='dd-toc' aria-label='Table of contents'>\n<p class='dd-toc-title'>In this guide</p>\n<ol>\n<li><a href='#leaks'>Where clinics lose patients</a></li>\n<li><a href='#booking'>Answer and book in minutes</a></li>\n<li><a href='#reminders'>Reminders that cut no-shows</a></li>\n<li><a href='#reviews'>Reviews and rebooking</a></li>\n<li><a href='#privacy'>Privacy and compliance</a></li>\n<li><a href='#launch'>Launch checklist and metrics</a></li>\n<li><a href='#faq'>FAQ</a></li>\n</ol>\n</nav>\n<h2 id='leaks'>1. Where clinics lose patients</h2>\n<p>Map the patient journey before you buy any tool. In most clinics it has five stages, and patients leak out at four of them.</p>\n<figure class='dd-fig'>\n<svg viewBox='0 0 640 236' role='img' aria-labelledby='fj1t fj1d' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'>\n<title id='fj1t'>Where a clinic loses patients</title>\n<desc id='fj1d'>Five stages from inquiry to booking, reminder, visit and review. Patients leak out at four points: slow replies to inquiries, slow back-and-forth while booking, no-shows after booking, and no review request after the visit.</desc>\n<defs><marker id='fj1a' viewBox='0 0 10 10' refX='9' refY='5' markerWidth='7' markerHeight='7' orient='auto'><path d='M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z' fill='#5b6470'/></marker></defs>\n<rect x='0' y='0' width='640' height='236' rx='14' fill='#f6f8fa'/>\n<text x='24' y='34' class='svg-k'>WHERE A CLINIC LOSES PATIENTS</text>\n<rect x='24' y='58' width='104' height='62' rx='10' fill='#007a66' stroke='#007a66'/>\n<text x='76.0' y='85' text-anchor='middle' class='svg-w'>Inquiry</text><text x='76.0' y='104' text-anchor='middle' class='svg-ws'>DM, call, form</text>\n<path d='M130 89 L144 89' stroke='#5b6470' stroke-width='1.6' marker-end='url(#fj1a)'/>\n<path d='M76.0 122 L76.0 150' stroke='#c2410c' stroke-width='1.6' stroke-dasharray='4 3' marker-end='url(#fj1a)'/>\n<rect x='28' y='156' width='96' height='30' rx='8' fill='#fff4ec' stroke='#c2410c'/><text x='76.0' y='176' text-anchor='middle' class='svg-o'>Slow reply</text>\n<rect x='146' y='58' width='104' height='62' rx='10' fill='#e8f4f1' stroke='#007a66'/>\n<text x='198.0' y='85' text-anchor='middle' class='svg-t'>Booking</text><text x='198.0' y='104' text-anchor='middle' class='svg-s'>date and time</text>\n<path d='M252 89 L266 89' stroke='#5b6470' stroke-width='1.6' marker-end='url(#fj1a)'/>\n<path d='M198.0 122 L198.0 150' stroke='#c2410c' stroke-width='1.6' stroke-dasharray='4 3' marker-end='url(#fj1a)'/>\n<rect x='150' y='156' width='96' height='30' rx='8' fill='#fff4ec' stroke='#c2410c'/><text x='198.0' y='176' text-anchor='middle' class='svg-o'>Slow booking</text>\n<rect x='268' y='58' width='104' height='62' rx='10' fill='#e8f4f1' stroke='#007a66'/>\n<text x='320.0' y='85' text-anchor='middle' class='svg-t'>Reminder</text><text x='320.0' y='104' text-anchor='middle' class='svg-s'>confirm or move</text>\n<path d='M374 89 L388 89' stroke='#5b6470' stroke-width='1.6' marker-end='url(#fj1a)'/>\n<path d='M320.0 122 L320.0 150' stroke='#c2410c' stroke-width='1.6' stroke-dasharray='4 3' marker-end='url(#fj1a)'/>\n<rect x='272' y='156' width='96' height='30' rx='8' fill='#fff4ec' stroke='#c2410c'/><text x='320.0' y='176' text-anchor='middle' class='svg-o'>No-show</text>\n<rect x='390' y='58' width='104' height='62' rx='10' fill='#e8f4f1' stroke='#007a66'/>\n<text x='442.0' y='85' text-anchor='middle' class='svg-t'>Visit</text><text x='442.0' y='104' text-anchor='middle' class='svg-s'>treatment</text>\n<path d='M496 89 L510 89' stroke='#5b6470' stroke-width='1.6' marker-end='url(#fj1a)'/>\n<rect x='512' y='58' width='104' height='62' rx='10' fill='#007a66' stroke='#007a66'/>\n<text x='564.0' y='85' text-anchor='middle' class='svg-w'>Review</text><text x='564.0' y='104' text-anchor='middle' class='svg-ws'>and rebook</text>\n<path d='M564.0 122 L564.0 150' stroke='#c2410c' stroke-width='1.6' stroke-dasharray='4 3' marker-end='url(#fj1a)'/>\n<rect x='516' y='156' width='96' height='30' rx='8' fill='#fff4ec' stroke='#c2410c'/><text x='564.0' y='176' text-anchor='middle' class='svg-o'>No review ask</text>\n<text x='24' y='216' class='svg-s'>Automation fixes the four leaks. Staff keep the treatment advice and the visit.</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>Figure 1.</b> Four leaks between the first message and the next booking. Each one has an automation fix.</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<div class='dd-table-wrap'><table>\n<thead><tr><th>Leak</th><th>What it looks like</th><th>Automation fix</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><b>Slow reply</b></td><td>An Instagram DM at 9 pm gets answered the next afternoon.</td><td>An AI agent answers common questions instantly, day or night.</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Slow booking</b></td><td>Five messages to agree on a date and time.</td><td>The agent offers real open slots from your calendar and books in the chat.</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>No-show</b></td><td>The patient forgets, or cannot come and does not tell you.</td><td>Automatic reminders with one-tap confirm or reschedule.</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>No review ask</b></td><td>A happy client leaves and is never asked for feedback.</td><td>An automatic feedback request after the visit, then a rebooking reminder.</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>Fix them in that order. Speed and booking bring revenue in, reminders protect it, and reviews bring the next patient.</p>\n<h2 id='booking'>2. Answer and book in minutes</h2>\n<p>Most clinic inquiries repeat: price ranges, treatment duration, downtime, location, parking, opening hours, payment options and “do you have a slot this Saturday?”. An AI agent trained on your own price list, treatment menu and policies answers these consistently and moves the patient to a booking.</p>\n<p>What the agent <b>should</b> do:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Answer factual questions from your approved treatment and price list.</li>\n<li>Ask two or three qualifying questions: which treatment, first visit or returning, preferred days.</li>\n<li>Offer open slots from your booking calendar and confirm the booking in the chat.</li>\n<li>Collect the details your front desk needs: name, contact, treatment of interest.</li>\n<li>Hand the conversation to a person when the patient asks for one, or when the question is medical.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>What the agent <b>must not</b> do: diagnose, say whether a treatment is safe for a specific person, recommend dosages, or comment on medical history, pregnancy or medication. Those questions go to a licensed member of your team.</p>\n<div class='dd-note'><span class='dd-note-label'>Dijae's rule</span>In a clinic, the AI books and the people advise. Write the handoff rule into the agent's instructions before anything else: any question about a person's health, suitability or results goes to your team, with the conversation and the patient's details already attached.</div>\n<p>If you are writing the agent's instructions, start from the clinic template in <a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/ai-agent-instructions-template'>How to Write AI Agent Instructions for Any Business</a>. It already includes the role, the booking steps and the medical handoff rules.</p>\n<h2 id='reminders'>3. Reminders that cut no-shows</h2>\n<p>Reminders are the highest-return automation in most clinics because the evidence is strong. A 2016 systematic review and meta-analysis in <i>BMJ Open</i> pooled 21 studies of digital appointment notifications, such as text messages, voice calls and email. Patients who received them attended 67% of appointments versus 54% without, and missed 15% versus 21%. That is about 25% fewer no-shows. The same review found that multiple notifications worked better than a single one.</p>\n<figure class='dd-fig'>\n<svg viewBox='0 0 640 312' role='img' aria-labelledby='fn1t fn1d' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'>\n<title id='fn1t'>Reminders and attendance</title>\n<desc id='fn1d'>Bar chart from a 2016 BMJ Open meta-analysis of 21 studies. Attendance was 67 percent with digital reminders versus 54 percent without. No-shows were 15 percent with reminders versus 21 percent without.</desc>\n<defs><marker id='fn1a' viewBox='0 0 10 10' refX='9' refY='5' markerWidth='7' markerHeight='7' orient='auto'><path d='M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z' fill='#5b6470'/></marker></defs>\n<rect x='0' y='0' width='640' height='312' rx='14' fill='#f6f8fa'/>\n<text x='24' y='34' class='svg-k'>BMJ OPEN META-ANALYSIS, 2016 (21 STUDIES)</text>\n<text x='24' y='64' class='svg-t'>Attended the appointment</text>\n<text x='24' y='96' class='svg-s'>Reminder sent</text><rect x='190' y='76' width='281' height='30' rx='6' fill='#007a66'/><text x='463' y='96' text-anchor='end' class='svg-w'>67%</text>\n<text x='24' y='134' class='svg-s'>No reminder</text><rect x='190' y='114' width='226' height='30' rx='6' fill='#5b9e90'/><text x='408' y='134' text-anchor='end' class='svg-w'>54%</text>\n<text x='24' y='182' class='svg-t'>Missed the appointment (no-show)</text>\n<text x='24' y='214' class='svg-s'>Reminder sent</text><rect x='190' y='194' width='63' height='30' rx='6' fill='#007a66'/><text x='245' y='214' text-anchor='end' class='svg-w'>15%</text>\n<text x='24' y='252' class='svg-s'>No reminder</text><rect x='190' y='232' width='88' height='30' rx='6' fill='#c2410c'/><text x='270' y='252' text-anchor='end' class='svg-w'>21%</text>\n<text x='24' y='292' class='svg-s'>Source: BMJ Open 2016;6:e012116. Electronic notifications (text, voice, email).</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>Figure 2.</b> Patients who got a digital reminder were about 25% less likely to miss their appointment.</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p>A schedule that works for most treatments:</p>\n<figure class='dd-fig'>\n<svg viewBox='0 0 640 196' role='img' aria-labelledby='fr1t fr1d' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'>\n<title id='fr1t'>A simple reminder schedule</title>\n<desc id='fr1d'>Timeline: instant confirmation when booked, a confirm-or-move message 48 hours before, prep instructions 24 hours before, address and parking 2 hours before. If the patient does not reply to the 48-hour message, staff call.</desc>\n<defs><marker id='fr1a' viewBox='0 0 10 10' refX='9' refY='5' markerWidth='7' markerHeight='7' orient='auto'><path d='M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z' fill='#5b6470'/></marker></defs>\n<rect x='0' y='0' width='640' height='196' rx='14' fill='#f6f8fa'/>\n<text x='24' y='34' class='svg-k'>A SIMPLE REMINDER SCHEDULE</text>\n<path d='M40 90 L612 90' stroke='#5b6470' stroke-width='1.6' marker-end='url(#fr1a)'/>\n<circle cx='70' cy='90' r='9' fill='#007a66'/><text x='70' y='66' text-anchor='middle' class='svg-t'>Booked</text><text x='70' y='120' text-anchor='middle' class='svg-s'>Instant confirmation</text>\n<circle cx='220' cy='90' r='9' fill='#007a66'/><text x='220' y='66' text-anchor='middle' class='svg-t'>48 hours before</text><text x='220' y='120' text-anchor='middle' class='svg-s'>Confirm, move or cancel</text>\n<circle cx='390' cy='90' r='9' fill='#007a66'/><text x='390' y='66' text-anchor='middle' class='svg-t'>24 hours before</text><text x='390' y='120' text-anchor='middle' class='svg-s'>Prep instructions</text>\n<circle cx='550' cy='90' r='9' fill='#007a66'/><text x='550' y='66' text-anchor='middle' class='svg-t'>2 hours before</text><text x='550' y='120' text-anchor='middle' class='svg-s'>Address and parking</text>\n<rect x='160' y='140' width='320' height='34' rx='8' fill='#fff4ec' stroke='#c2410c'/><text x='320' y='162' text-anchor='middle' class='svg-o'>No reply to the 48-hour message? Staff call.</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>Figure 3.</b> Every reminder gives the patient an easy way to confirm or reschedule. A freed slot can be offered to the waitlist.</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<div class='dd-code'><button class='dd-copy' type='button'>Copy</button><pre><code>48-HOUR REMINDER (example wording)\nHi [first name], this is [clinic name]. You are booked for\n[treatment] on [day] at [time].\n\nReply 1 to confirm\nReply 2 to reschedule\nReply 3 to cancel\n\nIf you need to change your booking, please let us know by\n[time] tomorrow so we can offer the slot to someone else.</code></pre></div>\n<p>Three details matter more than the wording. Make rescheduling as easy as confirming, because a moved appointment is better than a missed one. Send a waitlist offer automatically when someone cancels. And if a patient does not reply to the 48-hour message, have a person call; that patient is the most likely no-show.</p>\n<p>To see what this is worth, run the numbers with your own data. Every figure below is an <b>illustrative example</b>, not a benchmark.</p>\n<div class='dd-table-wrap'><table>\n<thead><tr><th>Input (example)</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>Appointments per month</td><td>300</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Current no-show rate</td><td>12%, so 36 missed appointments</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Average revenue per visit</td><td>$200</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Revenue from empty slots per month</b></td><td><b>$7,200</b> (36 × $200)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>No-shows reduced by a quarter</td><td>9 fewer missed appointments</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Revenue recovered per month</b></td><td><b>$1,800</b> (9 × $200)</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h2 id='reviews'>4. Reviews and rebooking</h2>\n<p>Patients check reviews before they book. In BrightLocal's 2025 Local Consumer Review Survey, only 4% of consumers said they never read online reviews of local businesses, and 96% said they are open to leaving a review for a business. Most clinics are not short of happy patients. They are short of a system that asks.</p>\n<p>A simple post-visit flow:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><b>Same day:</b> a thank-you message with aftercare instructions for the treatment.</li>\n<li><b>One to three days later:</b> a short feedback request with a direct link to your Google review page, sent to <b>every</b> patient.</li>\n<li><b>If the patient replies with a problem:</b> route it to the clinic manager right away and resolve it personally.</li>\n<li><b>At the treatment's natural interval:</b> a rebooking reminder, for example when a maintenance session is usually due.</li>\n</ol>\n<div class='dd-warn'><span class='dd-note-label'>Do not gate reviews</span>Google's review policy prohibits businesses from discouraging negative reviews or selectively asking only happy customers for reviews. It also prohibits offering discounts, free services or other incentives in exchange for a review. Ask everyone, the same way, and respond to every review.</div>\n<p>For reference, check Google's review policy <a href='https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/7400114?hl=en' rel='noopener' target='_blank'>here</a>.</p>\n<h2 id='privacy'>5. Privacy and compliance</h2>\n<p>Clinic automation handles personal data, and sometimes health data. Treat privacy as part of the design, not a final check.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Keep health details out of chat and text messages.</b> Reminders need a name, a time and a treatment type at most. Medical history, photos and consent forms belong in your clinic system, not in a chatbot.</li>\n<li><b>In the US, check whether HIPAA applies to your clinic.</b> If it does, any vendor that creates, stores or transmits protected health information for you must sign a business associate agreement (BAA) before you use it. Many chatbot and messaging tools do not sign one, so the safe design keeps protected health information out of those tools entirely.</li>\n<li><b>Use reasonable safeguards for messages.</b> HHS guidance allows providers to communicate with patients electronically when they apply reasonable safeguards, such as confirming contact details and limiting the information sent.</li>\n<li><b>Outside the US,</b> check your local privacy law for consent, data storage and marketing messages.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>This section is general guidance, not legal advice. Confirm your setup with your compliance advisor before launch.</p>\n<h2 id='launch'>6. Launch checklist and metrics</h2>\n<p>Launch in stages: instant replies and booking first, reminders second, reviews and rebooking third. Test each stage before you switch on the next one.</p>\n<div class='dd-code'><button class='dd-copy' type='button'>Copy</button><pre><code>CLINIC AUTOMATION TEST CHECKLIST\n[ ] Agent answers the 20 most common questions correctly\n[ ] Prices and treatment names match the current menu\n[ ] Medical questions (pregnancy, medication, allergies,\n    “is this safe for me?”) always hand off to a person\n[ ] Booking shows only real open slots and creates the\n    appointment in the clinic calendar\n[ ] Confirmation arrives instantly after booking\n[ ] Reply 1 / 2 / 3 on the reminder confirms, reschedules\n    and cancels correctly\n[ ] A cancellation triggers the waitlist offer\n[ ] No health details appear in any automated message\n[ ] Feedback request goes to every patient, not only happy ones\n[ ] Staff get notified of every handoff within minutes</code></pre></div>\n<div class='dd-table-wrap'><table>\n<thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>What it tells you</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><b>Time to first reply</b></td><td>Whether inquiries are answered while the patient is still interested.</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Inquiry-to-booking rate</b></td><td>Whether conversations turn into appointments.</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>No-show rate</b></td><td>Whether reminders are working. Compare with your rate before launch.</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Reviews per month</b></td><td>Whether the feedback flow is reaching patients.</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Rebooking rate</b></td><td>Whether patients come back for the next session.</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>Measure the first three for two weeks before launch, so you have a baseline. <a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/chatbot-roi-metrics'>The 5 chatbot ROI metrics</a> shows how to turn them into one monthly number.</p>\n<p>An honest limitation: automation cannot fix a full calendar, a pricing problem or a poor patient experience. Reminders reduce no-shows but do not remove them, and some patients will always prefer a phone call. Keep a person reachable at every step.</p>\n<h2 id='faq'>Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>Can an AI chatbot give treatment advice to patients?</h3>\n<p>No. Use the AI for information, booking and reminders. Any question about a person's health, suitability for a treatment or expected results should go to a licensed member of your team.</p>\n<h3>Which channel should clinic reminders use?</h3>\n<p>Use the channel your patients already answer: text message, WhatsApp, Messenger or email. Research on digital reminders found that multiple notifications work better than one, so combine a 48-hour and a same-day message.</p>\n<h3>Is it allowed to ask only happy patients for Google reviews?</h3>\n<p>No. Google's policy prohibits selectively soliciting positive reviews and discouraging negative ones. Send the same request to every patient and handle complaints personally.</p>\n<h3>What should a clinic automate first?</h3>\n<p>Instant replies and booking, because they bring revenue in. Then reminders, because they protect it. Then reviews and rebooking, because they bring the next patient.</p>\n<div class='dd-cta'>\n<p class='dd-cta-title'>Tools that fit clinics and med spas</p>\n<p>For clinics in the US and Canada that want booking calendars, text and email reminders and review requests in one place, I recommend <a href='https://www.gohighlevel.com/?fp_ref=dijae-044b83' rel='sponsored nofollow'>GoHighLevel</a>. For Instagram DM automation, <a href='https://manychat.partnerlinks.io/rozuomtj4677' rel='sponsored nofollow'>ManyChat</a>. For Messenger-first clinics in the Philippines and Southeast Asia, <a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/botcake' rel='sponsored nofollow'>Botcake</a> and <a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/pancake' rel='sponsored nofollow'>Pancake</a> (coupon <b>CHAMP20</b> for 20% off all Pancake plans plus 30 days free for new Pancake customers or a new billing account). These are affiliate links.</p>\n<p>Want this mapped for your clinic? <a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/book'>Book a free AI Automation Blueprint call</a>.</p>\n</div>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ol class='dd-refs'>\n<li><a href='https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27798006/' rel='noopener' target='_blank'>Using digital notifications to improve attendance in clinic: systematic review and meta-analysis</a>. <i>BMJ Open</i>, 2016;6(10):e012116.</li>\n<li><a href='https://www.brightlocal.com/research/local-consumer-review-survey-2025/' rel='noopener' target='_blank'>Local Consumer Review Survey 2025</a>. BrightLocal.</li>\n<li><a href='https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/7400114?hl=en' rel='noopener' target='_blank'>Fake engagement policy (reviews)</a>. Google Maps user-generated content policy. Accessed October 2026.</li>\n<li><a href='https://www.hhs.gov/hipaa/for-professionals/privacy/guidance/business-associates/index.html' rel='noopener' target='_blank'>Business Associates</a>. U.S. Department of Health and Human Services. Accessed October 2026.</li>\n<li><a href='https://www.hhs.gov/hipaa/for-professionals/faq/570/does-hipaa-permit-health-care-providers-to-use-email-to-discuss-health-issues-with-patients/index.html' rel='noopener' target='_blank'>Does HIPAA permit health care providers to use e-mail to discuss health issues with patients?</a> HHS FAQ. Accessed October 2026.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Keep reading</h2>\n<ul class='dd-more'>\n<li><a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/ai-agent-instructions-template'>How to Write AI Agent Instructions for Any Business (Templates Inside)</a></li>\n<li><a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/how-to-test-an-ai-chatbot'>How to Test an AI Chatbot Before It Talks to Your Customers</a></li>\n<li><a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/automate-lead-follow-up'>How to Automate Lead Follow-Up With AI</a></li>\n<li><a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/blog'>See all posts on the blog</a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n"},"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"height":9208,"left":160,"top":450,"width":640}},"mobile":{"styles":{"height":11794,"left":20,"top":388,"width":380}}}},{"id":"h_css2121","type":"html-box","specials":{"html":"&lt;style&gt;.dd-article ul{list-style:disc outside !important}.dd-article ol{list-style:decimal outside !important}.dd-article li{display:list-item !important}.dd-article ul ul{list-style:circle outside !important}&lt;/style&gt;"},"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"height":1,"left":160,"top":9705,"width":1}},"mobile":{"styles":{"height":1,"left":20,"top":12221,"width":1}}}}]},{"id":"sec_2141","type":"section","responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"background":"rgba(247,248,250,1)","height":402}},"mobile":{"styles":{"background":"rgba(247,248,250,1)","height":508}}},"children":[{"id":"t_2142","type":"text-block","specials":{"tag":"h2","text":"Get one practical idea like this every week"},"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(26,26,26,1)","fontSize":26,"fontWeight":"800","height":69,"left":160,"lineHeight":"1.25","textAlign":"left","top":56,"width":640}},"mobile":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(26,26,26,1)","fontSize":22,"fontWeight":"800","height":59,"left":20,"lineHeight":"1.25","textAlign":"left","top":40,"width":380}}}},{"id":"t_2143","type":"text-block","specials":{"text":"Join the free newsletter on AI agents, automation and turning your skills into income. Prefer video? Watch the walkthroughs on <a hr